data directory; this is proportionate to corpus search, but users should expect network and disk use.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The setup script downloads the chinese-poetry dataset from GitHub without pinning a commit or verifying a checksum, so installed corpus contents can change after review.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Activation wording is broad and the materials are Chinese-only, which may affect routing or language expectations, but these are usability and scoping notes rather than evidence of unsafe intent.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No startup hooks, services, scheduled tasks, memory writes, credential reads, privilege escalation, or cross-session backdoor behavior were found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill purpose is clearly poetry generation and poetry lookup, and the prompt, README, and skill metadata all align to that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, be aware that setup.sh downloads a large public dataset from GitHub and does not pin or verify the exact revision. This is not evidence of malicious behavior, but users who need reproducible or high-integrity results should pin a reviewed commit or verify the dataset themselves.","findings":"[TM1] expected: The rm -rf use is confined to paths under the skill's data directory after cloning and appears to remove dataset repository metadata and unneeded files, not arbitrary user data.\n[SQP-1] expected: Broad natural-language poetry triggers are consistent with a prompt-based poetry skill, though narrower activation or clarification would reduce accidental invocation.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese-only instructions match the Chinese classical poetry domain, but the skill should ideally document language expectations or follow the user's preferred language when practical.\n[T08] expected: Using the public chinese-poetry repository is purpose-aligned, but cloning the mutable default branch without integrity verification is a supply-chain integrity weakness for corpus contents.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789189428211}}}}}